30,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It's worse than I thought. People are shifting other bikes just to leave, and some spots are completely exposed to rain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The building has almost no funds for improvements. Also, external parking is quite expensive and has a long waiting list.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The same people have held the best spots for years without any review. However, daily riders are open to paying for a spot.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Charging money can cause real bitterness. In the next block, it led to people skipping meetings and avoiding neighbors.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Managing payments is a lot of tedious paperwork. Also, those fancy double-tier racks are actually quite a pain to use.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@George, if the same people always have the dry spots, that explains the tension.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, while bitterness is a risk, the fact that external parking is full means we must solve this internally.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Asuka, yes, the lack of review is the core issue. We need a system that resets.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, but a rigid payment system might be too cold for a small building like ours.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, if the racks are hard to use, maybe we shouldn't go for the double-tier option.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we don't change the allocation, the ""shoving matches"" in the morning will only get worse.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We need a solution that is financially sustainable without requiring a massive levy.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,The daily riders' willingness to pay is an interesting point. It separates need from mere preference.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,I still worry about the social cost. A lottery is fairer and less likely to cause long-term grudges.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,I just don't want to be the one stuck doing three hours of bookkeeping a month!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
